          {
            "extracted_values": {
              "direction": "left_to_right",
              "mechanism_id": 1,
              "mechanism_text": "The ground state of the enzyme contains a covalent linkage between Lys39 and the PLP cofactor. The reaction proceeds via an initial transldimination in which the substrate alanine eliminates Lys39 from PLP. In the L-Ala to D-Ala direction Tyr265B abstracts a proton from the alpha carbon of the alanine (and Lys39 deprotonates water). Water deprotonates Tyr265B. The carbanionic intermediate deprotonates Lys39. In the final steps, a second transaldimination occurs, eliminating the product and returning the protein to its ground state. In the D-Ala to L-Ala direction, the roles of Tyr265B and Lys39 are reversed. The tyrosine and the lysine residues are on opposite sides of the PLP cofactor.",
              "step_1_text": "The amine of the substrate L-alanine attacks the PLP cofactor in a nucleophilic addition and the bound Lys39 deprotonates the newly attached amine.",
              "step_6_text": "The secondary amine that results from the initial attack initiates an elimination of the covalently bound product, resulting in D-alanine and the regenerated PLP cofactor."
            },
